WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.275
Here's the decision table, and every row
is design guidance, not an endorsement.

2
00:00:05.275 --> 00:00:09.405
If you're mostly on premises with a
small cloud footprint, Trinzic plus

3
00:00:09.405 --> 00:00:13.963
native cloud resolvers and conditional
forwarding is the lowest-cost start.

4
00:00:13.963 --> 00:00:17.300
Hybrid with one cloud,
add a vNIOS pair in a hub

5
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:21.088
network so resolution stays
local if the WAN fails.

6
00:00:21.088 --> 00:00:23.741
Multi-cloud at FedRAMP Moderate and below,

7
00:00:23.741 --> 00:00:26.927
consider Universal DDI
through Government Cloud,

8
00:00:26.927 --> 00:00:31.098
whether those workloads run in
commercial regions or in GovCloud;

9
00:00:31.098 --> 00:00:34.587
there, confirm which features
Infoblox supports first.

10
00:00:34.587 --> 00:00:38.166
And for FedRAMP High systems,
stay with options A and C,

11
00:00:38.166 --> 00:00:41.175
because Infoblox's
service is Moderate-only.

12
00:00:41.175 --> 00:00:45.183
In short: Trinzic plus native
resolvers as the baseline,

13
00:00:45.183 --> 00:00:50.110
with vNIOS and Universal DDI added
only where they earn their place.
